# Animation Patterns with Framer Motion

## Animation Components
The project uses custom animation components from [src/components/animations](mdc:src/components/animations):

### Core Animation Components
```typescript
import { 
  FadeInUp, 
  StaggerContainer, 
  FloatingCard, 
  PulsingBadge 
} from "@/components/animations";
```

## Standard Animation Patterns

### Page Entry Animations
Use `FadeInUp` for consistent page entry animations:

```typescript
<FadeInUp>
  <section className="container mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <div className="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center space-y-6">
      <FadeInUp delay={0.1}>
        <Badge variant="secondary">{badgeText}</Badge>
      </FadeInUp>
      
      <FadeInUp delay={0.2}>
        <h1 className="text-4xl font-bold">{title}</h1>
      </FadeInUp>
      
      <FadeInUp delay={0.3}>
        <p className="text-xl text-muted-foreground">{description}</p>
      </FadeInUp>
    </div>
  </section>
</FadeInUp>
```

### Staggered List Animations
Use `StaggerContainer` for animating lists and grids:

```typescript
<StaggerContainer>
  {items.map((item, index) => (
    <FadeInUp key={item.id} delay={index * 0.1}>
      <Card>
        <CardContent>{item.content}</CardContent>
      </Card>
    </FadeInUp>
  ))}
</StaggerContainer>
```

### Floating Card Effects
Use `FloatingCard` for interactive card components:

```typescript
<FloatingCard>
  <Card className="hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow">
    <CardHeader>
      <CardTitle>Card Title</CardTitle>
    </CardHeader>
    <CardContent>
      Card content with floating animation
    </CardContent>
  </Card>
</FloatingCard>
```

### Pulsing Badge Effects
Use `PulsingBadge` for attention-grabbing elements:

```typescript
<PulsingBadge>
  <Badge variant="secondary" className="text-sm">
    New Feature
  </Badge>
</PulsingBadge>
```

## Interactive Animations

### Button Hover Effects
```typescript
import { motion } from "framer-motion";

<motion.div
  whileHover={{
    scale: 1.05,
    y: -2,
    transition: { duration: 0.2 },
  }}
  whileTap={{ scale: 0.95 }}
>
  <Button size="lg" asChild>
    <Link href="/path">Button Text</Link>
  </Button>
</motion.div>
```

### Card Hover Animations
```typescript
<motion.div
  whileHover={{
    scale: 1.02,
    y: -4,
    transition: { duration: 0.2 },
  }}
  className="cursor-pointer"
>
  <Card className="transition-shadow hover:shadow-lg">
    {/* Card content */}
  </Card>
</motion.div>
```

## Animation Timing

### Standard Delays
- Initial content: `delay={0.1}`
- Secondary content: `delay={0.2}`
- Tertiary content: `delay={0.3}`
- List items: `delay={index * 0.1}`

### Transition Durations
- Quick interactions: `duration: 0.2`
- Page transitions: `duration: 0.3`
- Complex animations: `duration: 0.5`

## Performance Considerations

### Reduce Motion
Always respect user preferences:

```typescript
import { useReducedMotion } from "framer-motion";

const shouldReduceMotion = useReducedMotion();

<motion.div
  animate={shouldReduceMotion ? {} : { opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
  transition={shouldReduceMotion ? {} : { duration: 0.3 }}
>
  Content
</motion.div>
```

### Optimize Animations
- Use `transform` and `opacity` for smooth animations
- Avoid animating layout properties
- Use `will-change` CSS property sparingly
- Consider using `layout` prop for layout animations

## Custom Animation Variants

### Page Transitions
```typescript
const pageVariants = {
  initial: { opacity: 0, y: 20 },
  animate: { opacity: 1, y: 0 },
  exit: { opacity: 0, y: -20 }
};

<motion.div
  variants={pageVariants}
  initial="initial"
  animate="animate"
  exit="exit"
  transition={{ duration: 0.3 }}
>
  Page content
</motion.div>
```

### Loading States
```typescript
const loadingVariants = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0 },
  visible: { opacity: 1 },
  exit: { opacity: 0 }
};

<motion.div
  variants={loadingVariants}
  initial="hidden"
  animate="visible"
  exit="exit"
>
  Loading content
</motion.div>
```

## Animation Guidelines
- Keep animations subtle and purposeful
- Maintain consistency across the site
- Test on different devices and browsers
- Consider accessibility and reduced motion preferences
- Use animations to guide user attention, not distract